Conclusions for part 2:
    Effect of NN interaction depends on the core-neutron state energy. Virtually no effect on a
    core + continum coupling state, and smaller effects on the lightly bound n + n state, large effect
    on the deeply bound state. In the distinquishable PP calculation the 2(2s) state nearly doubles in energy
    between max and min scattering values, suggests that care does need to be taken when chosing these values
    and paramaterising just off of scattering length is not enough. 
    For the same S calculation theres virtually no change, sort of as expected for core + continum coupling.
